  "notes": "## CatLab Studio 1.0.9\n\nThis release focuses on reliable daily use for the lab, especially on Windows.\n\n### What changed\n\n- Prompts can be queued while the current turn keeps running; sending the next instruction no longer interrupts active work.\n- Failed tool calls are recoverable and no longer leave the conversation permanently stuck.\n- Team-managed MCP and knowledge services are configured automatically after platform sign-in; only services that truly require a personal key still ask for one.\n- Settings and first-run readiness were simplified, including clearer UMA licence/setup status, data-source state, compute-node boundaries, and fewer redundant setup banners.\n- Model and sub-agent controls now follow the platform model catalogue and support per-agent model selection. GPT-6 Astra metadata includes its 1,050,000-token context window and adjustable reasoning effort.\n- CatLab branding and icons were refreshed across the Windows/macOS app and the web download/API surfaces.\n\n### Install and first launch\n\n**Windows** — download `CatLab.Studio_1.0.9_x64-setup.exe`. It installs per user and does not require administrator rights. If SmartScreen appears, choose **More info → Run anyway**. Install over the existing version to retain sessions and settings.\n\n**macOS (Apple Silicon, macOS 13+)** — open the DMG and drag **CatLab Studio** into Applications. This build is ad-hoc signed because the project has no Apple Developer account; it is not Developer ID-signed or notarized. On first launch, right-click the app and choose **Open**, or run `xattr -dr com.apple.quarantine '/Applications/CatLab Studio.app'`.\n\nIn-app update checks report that a newer version exists; they do not install it automatically.\n",
